{title: 678 - God Be in My Head}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #678 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 678}
{meta: category Sentences and Responses - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]God be in [F#m]my [G#dim]head, [E/B]and [Bm]in my understanding;
[E]God be in [F#m]mine [G#dim]eyes, [Bm]and [E]in [D/A]my [C#m/G#]looking;
[E]God [F#m]be [G#dim]in [A]my [C#m/G#]mouth, [F#m]and in my [E]speaking;
[E]God be [A]in [C#7]my [F#m/C#]heart, [D/F#]and [F#m]in [A7]my thinking;
[A]God be [D/A]at [A7/G]mine end, [D/A]and at my [Bm]departing.
{end_of_verse}
